:CS66 a :CS65,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "BRD_Prevalence"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The prevalence of Bovine Respiratory Disease (BRD) in cattle varies significantly across different regions, age groups, and diagnostic methods. BRD is estimated to affect 2.1% to 20.2% of cattle, with higher rates observed in winter months. The disease is a leading cause of morbidity and mortality in pre-weaned dairy calves, and its economic impact is substantial, leading to mortality, reduced growth, and lower carcass value." .

:CS67 a :CS65,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "PRDC_Prevalence"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The prevalence of Porcine Respiratory Disease Complex (PRDC)" .

